  "title": "Japan's Shinto Shrine Visit Sparks Controversy Amid WWII Wartime",
  "summary": "Japan's Defence Minister Koizumi visits the Yasukuni Shrine, which commemorates the 81st anniversary of Japan's WWII surrender. The visit comes amid tensions with China and South Korea, as the shrine's inclusion of war criminals from World War II has sparked criticism.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Japanese government skipped the Yasukuni Shrine visit to avoid diplomatic tensions with China and South Korea.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The shrine was controversial due to its inclusion of 14 convicted Japanese war criminals from World War II.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Japan has long condemned its wartime atrocities and continues to emphasize its commitment to global peace.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
